Message-ID: <9B884D5E-44FA-48A7-968F-B5C375B035CD@r-project.org>


On Dec 18, 2011, at 7:00 PM, Dario Strbenac wrote:

> In R, it's possible to give it incomplete expressions, and it will wait for more input before running. Can this be done with JRI ?
> 
> Can something like this work as expected ?
> 
>            rExec.eval("x <- numeric()");
>            rExec.eval("for(i in 1:5)");
>            rExec.eval("x <- c(x, i)");
>            System.out.println(rExec.eval("print(x)"));
> 

By definition, no. R can only evaluate complete expressions. Even in the R console the expression is not evaluated until it is complete (i.e. when you type "for(i in 1:10)" in R it is *not* evaluated since it doesn't parse into an expression).

Cheers,
Simon

